  ProseChapter(
    'Gold as a Hedge Against Inflation and Crisis',
    [
      ProseSection(
        'The promises: haven, inflation hedge, insurance',
        'Of gold three things are often said: that it is a safe haven '
            'in a crisis, a hedge against inflation, and a kind of '
            'insurance for one\'s wealth. These three promises sound '
            'similar, but they mean different things.\n\n'
            'A haven is supposed to hold when other things fall. An '
            'inflation hedge is supposed to preserve purchasing power when '
            'money loses value. An insurance usually costs something and '
            'pays off only in the event of damage. Whether gold delivers '
            'all of this depends on the time span over which one asks.',
      ),
      ProseSection(
        'What the long run shows',
        'Over very long periods, gold has held its purchasing power '
            'remarkably well — this is shown against grain in the chapter '
            '"Does Gold Hold Its Value?"\n\n'
            'But it does not follow from this that gold compensates for '
            'every loss of monetary value. The protection takes hold over '
            'very long horizons, over which hardly anyone invests their '
            'money. "In the long run" and "within my investing lifetime" '
            'are two different time spans.',
      ),
      ProseSection(
        'What the short run shows',
        'Over years and decades, gold can lose value in real terms. '
            'There were long stretches in which gold did not compensate for '
            'inflation, and others in which it far surpassed it. A reliable '
            'lockstep with prices from one year to the next does not '
            'exist.\n\n'
            'The "safe haven" too depends on the situation. In some crises '
            'gold rose while stocks fell. But in a panic over cash, many '
            'sold their gold as well to get hold of liquidity — then it '
            'fell along with the rest.',
        illustrationId: 'werte/inflation-horizon',
      ),
      ProseSection(
        'Gold in the portfolio: diversifier, not return engine',
        'In the world of investing, gold is usually regarded as an '
            'admixture that spreads risk, not as a source of high returns. '
            'It often moves differently from stocks and bonds, and that is '
            'precisely what makes it useful as a mix.\n\n'
            'One point belongs here: gold pays no interest and no dividend. '
            'A bar lies there and does not multiply on its own. Whoever '
            'holds gold is betting on the preservation of value, not on a '
            'running yield.',
      ),
      ProseSection(
        'Protection over which time span?',
        'The sentence "gold always protects against inflation" does not '
            'hit the matter. Over very long periods the purchasing power '
            'stays within the same order of magnitude; over years and '
            'decades gold can lose in real terms. Which of the two '
            'prospects counts is decided by the time span over which one '
            'asks.\n\n'
            'Fixed return figures, correlations, or a "correct" gold share '
            'in one\'s wealth are deliberately not stated here — they '
            'depend on the period and the situation. Whoever promotes the '
            'gold trade, industry associations for instance, is in this a '
            'party with an interest of its own.',
      ),
    ],
    sources: [
      Source(
